      </pen>
    </plot>
    <monitor x="710" precision="2" y="113" height="60" fontSize="11" width="120" display="mean speed">mean [ speed ] of cars</monitor>
    <monitor x="710" precision="0" y="183" height="60" fontSize="11" width="120" display="stopped cars">count cars with [ speed = 0 ]</monitor>
    <chooser x="845" y="113" height="60" variable="talk" current="0" width="250" display="talk">
      <choice type="string" value="none"></choice>
      <choice type="string" value="brake lights"></choice>
      <choice type="string" value="marks"></choice>
      <choice type="string" value="blackboard"></choice>
      <choice type="string" value="unicast"></choice>
      <choice type="string" value="broadcast"></choice>
      <choice type="string" value="subscribe"></choice>
      <choice type="string" value="request"></choice>
      <choice type="string" value="query"></choice>
    </chooser>
    <slider x="845" step="1" y="178" max="30" width="250" display="talk-range" height="50" min="1" direction="Horizontal" default="15.0" variable="talk-range" units="cells"></slider>
    <slider x="845" step="0.05" y="233" max="1" width="250" display="p-loss" height="50" min="0" direction="Horizontal" default="0.0" variable="p-loss"></slider>
    <slider x="845" step="0.05" y="288" max="1" width="250" display="evaporation" height="50" min="0" direction="Horizontal" default="0.2" variable="evaporation"></slider>
    <slider x="845" step="1" y="343" max="3" width="250" display="ambulances" height="50" min="1" direction="Horizontal" default="1.0" variable="ambulances"></slider>
    <switch x="845" y="398" height="40" on="false" variable="deadline?" width="120" display="deadline?"></switch>
    <switch x="975" y="398" height="40" on="false" variable="trace?" width="120" display="trace?"></switch>
    <monitor x="710" precision="0" y="253" height="60" fontSize="11" width="120" display="messages / tick">sent</monitor>
    <monitor x="710" precision="0" y="323" height="60" fontSize="11" width="120" display="hard brakes / tick">hard-brakes</monitor>
    <monitor x="710" precision="2" y="393" height="60" fontSize="11" width="120" display="ambulance speed">ambulance-speed</monitor>
  </widgets>
  <info><![CDATA[## WHAT IS IT?

The ring road of lab 1 (Nagel-Schreckenberg: accelerate, never drive into what is ahead, sometimes brake for no reason), where cars can also hear about the road ahead. The chooser TALK picks one way of communicating: brake lights (signal), marks (stigmergy), blackboard (shared memory), unicast, broadcast, subscribe (publish/subscribe with the light), request (FIPA-Request between an ambulance and the light), query (query-ref to the light, section 7.1 of the lab sheet).

## HOW IT WORKS

Every tick: the light reads its mail and switches; every car listens and decides; every car moves; every car tells. What is told at tick t is heard at tick t + 1. What a car hears only lowers its ADVICE (the speed it allows itself); rule 2 (perception) still prevents every collision.

## HOW TO USE IT

Choose TALK, press SETUP, then GO. Yellow arcs: messages of this tick. Turquoise cell under a car: it slowed down because of what it heard. Orange: marks on the road. Violet: notes on the blackboard. Blue band: radio range of a broadcast. Green arcs: subscriptions. Blue car: the ambulance.

In the Command Center, `measure 10` averages 10 runs of 800 ticks (hard brakes / tick, messages / tick, mean speed); `measure-ambulance 10` gives the ambulance speed. TRACE? prints every message (and whether it was lost). DEADLINE? (7.2): the ambulance asks again 3 ticks after an unanswered request. AMBULANCES (7.3): number of ambulances with TALK on request.
]]></info>
